## Fix v1 (flush and DISCARD the tail) — rejected, receipts in bench/z49/receipts/fix-v1-discarded/
# Discarding the tail turns a token whose bytes end in an incomplete sequence into a counterfeit character:
#   o200k id 439 = bytes d0 be d0 ("о" + dangling lead byte)  -> decoded as "о"   (encode("о") = [317])
#   id 671 = e1 83 90 e1 83 -> "ა";  id 1049 = e5 bd a9 e7 a5 -> "彩";  id 5198 -> "្"
# The glyph pools then held duplicates ("о" twice in cyrillic, "彩" twice in cjk), their order shifted, and the
# ARIADNE default arm on gh-followers-20 (plain, all-ASCII) went from 840 to 1054 (DAEDALUS 840 -> 922).

## Fix v2 (final): flush before, and APPEND the final flush to the result = non-streaming semantics
#   decodeIds([439]) = "о\uFFFD" (excluded from every script pool, as it should be)
#   pools: identical to the leaky pools minus the counterfeit glyphs (hangul 679->677, cjk 2517->2515, polyglot 802->799, khmer 67->66), no duplicates, same order
#   gh-followers-20 plain: 840 / 840 (two calls, one process)     — reference unchanged
#   gh-tags-20 composed:   706 / 706 / 706                          — was 787 / 706 / 706 (and 869 after a plain run)
# Regression probe: OMEGA_DET=1 bench/tmp/run.sh bench/z49/det-leak.ts  -> bench/z49/receipts/fixed/det-leak-after.log
